          "replacement": "# Corpus x86 3820 selected-entry preparation R4\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 2,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 3,
          "old_text_sha256": "315ca590dcd861ad808239a50522775bc49375450d94d84cca56d75146944680",
          "replacement": "Preparation only. AS OF AUTHOR FREEZE, Root and independent full-code preflight and separate own-fixture-R4 selection remain pending. No Ghidra, Java/compiler, decoder, original slice extraction/import or guest execution occurred in R4 preparation. The only construction was one analyst-owned synthetic Mach-O DATA builder run.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 4,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 5,
          "old_text_sha256": "5c66f21199c9b095d17499c23ebfe0b3c537778f8918c55ec908ac25fa61a4d7",
          "replacement": "The fixed ordered entries are `0x23b0` (retained control nomination) and `0x3820` (new processing-candidate nomination), each with an explicitly Root-selected 1,024-byte body/output limit. Linker-start membership and neighbor `0x39a0` provide navigation only. Their gap is not an extent, read limit, callability or processing-role proof. Whole thin Program data/signatures remain available internally; the bound limits selected body/listing/C output, not every internal read. No third entry, autoexpansion, callee export or whole-program analysis.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 6,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 7,
          "old_text_sha256": "d827d67451284eff4c66566f6591484e008548d55db82452f377cf9002f78c2f",
          "replacement": "An initial instruction required byte-identical R3 Java, which conflicts with its hardcoded second-entry guards. Before creating R4 files the author identified that conflict. Root expressly authorized exactly two necessary Java address-literal replacements: second seed guard `0x29c0` to `0x3820`, and permitted export entry `0x29c0L` to `0x3820L`. All other Java bytes remain exact after reversing those two literals: six strict machine predicates and diagnostic, two-entry/window/body/boundary/overlap/control-flow/partial-C/resource/noanalysis and success rules stay unchanged.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 8,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 9,
          "old_text_sha256": "7dcb3cdee33a465878818fa3daf47c73beaf253127b21eed07f2f4d84d7faa60",
          "replacement": "The driver changes only three fixed R4 paths, the second seed address and navigation label, and the owned fixture SHA/length. Original thin identity remains 250,352 bytes, SHA-256 `03be50fae8abee39dcaafec743d82ab4c908d548977354528aa1b8dd3919b00d`, universal offset16,384. The R3 late override environment and all other environment/JDK/heap/pool/supervision/receipt logic are unchanged.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 10,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 11,
          "old_text_sha256": "3bfc3e458f56917f4b2b05de6972f81661115f45bc5272a38f0c4c4cb5f537fb",
          "replacement": "The new owned fixture is 16,384 bytes: TEXT `[0,0x4000)`, section `[0x2000,0x4000)`, `MOV EAX,42; RET` at `0x23b0` and `XOR EAX,EAX; RET` at `0x3820`. Each selected window fits within that section. Expected synthetic bodies remain six/three bytes and two instructions. The fixture contains no original bytes and is never executed as guest code. Its new SHA is `b6d176792b5ce2e12bfeb0546e469e7922e902a9f4d9dff9819a5199e22dad03`.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 12,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 13,
          "old_text_sha256": "487a8ce8e537642523de2d3e57533b16ce48520a086b08f1fac3e01c88516f05",
          "replacement": "Resources stay 4 GiB heap, 6 GiB aggregate RSS, 3 GiB disk floor, CPU/pool two, 180-second tool supervision and 60 seconds per entry. Analysis is explicitly disabled in Java and launcher. Root's separate outer coordinator must retain pretry, interruption, owned process-group cleanup and catastrophic-I/O outcomes. Sampling and PID/start-string ownership remain finite limits. One attempt, no automatic retry.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_line_start_zero": 14,
          "old_line_end_exclusive": 15,
          "old_text_sha256": "ffba0d6dab21bd650cb5dc5eb69b9c876c735ddd3a0dd036110db911263ab6c8",
          "replacement": "After full Root and independent code reviews, Root must separately select a new fixture-R4 run, then obtain independent actual review of its exact two successful exports. Only a later separate actual-R4 selection may read/extract/import original bytes. R3 success does not bypass the new current-fixture gate. The future interface is `python3 -B run-selected.py fixture|actual PREPARATION_SHA SELECTION_SHA`; paths acquire the exclusive R4 suffix, never overwrite old artifacts. This describes a future interface, not a launch request.\n\n[inputs.json](inputs.json) pins immutable prior preparation/history, current reviewed R3 original/fixture manifests and peers, and the reviewed 3820 metadata nomination. [source-delta.json](source-delta.json) reconstructs every changed source/config/auxiliary plus the own builder, without copying old archives. The original 174 modal omissions, two note72 omissions, requirements/cases and all unknown application scope remain unchanged.\n\nRead [check.py](check.py) fully before `python3 -B check.py --check`. It uses only five fully read pure config/scope definitions, never driver import/main/source extraction/tool/resource functions. It checks positive fixture geometry, exact two Java and seven driver substitutions, inherited 15 scope rejections plus explicit wrong-owned-SHA and old-second-seed rejection, strict guard/environment preservation, and all pins/deltas. Future R4 destinations must be absent. No native outcome, processing receiver mapping, new criterion/grade or compatibility completion is claimed.\n"
        }
      ]
